            <ArticleTitle>Giant coronary artery aneurysm presenting as a mediastinal mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1307-8, A11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An asymptomatic mediastinal mass in a 72-year-old man was imaged by computer tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, and coronary arteriography, revealing a giant atheromatous aneurysm of the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
